      "content": "it's just that everything feels so... irreversible. like, people talk about \"sustainability\" or \"policy changes\" but it feels like trying to put out a forest fire with a water pistol. how are we supposed to justify building a life, or having a family, or even just sticking around for the next forty years when the foundation is basically crumbling? it feels like we're all just being forced to watch a horror movie that never ends.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
